<h1>Networking &amp; HTTP</h1>
<p>Multiplayer is host-authoritative: the host owns spawning, ownership, and message validation. HTTP/HTTPS is available separately for REST backends and is async so gameplay never blocks.</p>

<h2>Network contract</h2>
<p>Declare a contract asset in the project:</p>
<pre><code>"network_contract": "asset://network/arena_contract"</code></pre>
<p>The <code>NetworkContract</code> asset is the single source of network rules: which prefabs the server may spawn, who may write which fields, message names and directions, size and rate limits, and payload schemas. Both sides hash the contract at session setup and refuse to start on mismatch.</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Values</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Senders / writers</td><td><code>server</code>, <code>owner</code>, <code>all</code></td><td>Who may spawn or write a replicated field</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Disconnect</td><td><code>despawn</code>, <code>return_to_server</code>, <code>transfer_by_game_policy</code></td><td>What happens to that player’s entities</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Message targets</td><td><code>owned_entity</code>, <code>entity</code>, <code>none</code></td><td>What the message is addressed to</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Session flow</h2>
<pre><code>local NetworkSession = require("demi.network.session")

-- Host:
NetworkSession.host(39420)                       -- returns true or nil, err
NetworkSession.start_session({
    scene_id = "scene://game",
    seed     = 42,
})

-- Client:
NetworkSession.connect("127.0.0.1", 39420)       -- returns true or nil, err</code></pre>
<p>Once running, pump the session every frame:</p>
<pre><code>function Game:on_update(dt)
    local events = NetworkSession.process_events()
    -- events is an array of validated contract messages
    for _, e in ipairs(events) do
        print(e.name, e.sender_id)
    end

    NetworkSession.update_entity(network_id, dt)
end</code></pre>
<p><code>process_events</code> returns the validated messages received since the last call (empty array when idle). Invalid or unauthorized traffic is rejected before Lua sees it. <code>update_entity</code> captures the contract-declared replicated fields for one entity.</p>
<p>Lifecycle phases: <code>closed</code> → <code>connected</code> → <code>authenticated</code> → <code>ready</code> → <code>active</code>, plus <code>reconnecting</code>. Query status with:</p>
<pre><code>local d = NetworkSession.diagnostics()
-- d.phase, d.epoch, d.contract_hash, plus send/receive counters

print(NetworkSession.is_connected())   -- boolean
print(NetworkSession.is_host())        -- boolean
print(NetworkSession.sender_id())      -- this peer’s ID
print(NetworkSession.current_session())-- session info table or nil</code></pre>

<h2>Authority and spawning</h2>
<pre><code>-- Host only:
local id = NetworkSession.spawn(prefab_key, entity_id, owner)
NetworkSession.transfer(network_id, new_owner)
NetworkSession.despawn(network_id)

if NetworkSession.has_authority(network_id) then
    -- safe to apply local gameplay for this entity
end

local owner = NetworkSession.owner(network_id)
local nid = NetworkSession.network_id_for_owner(owner_id)
NetworkSession.bind_local_entity(entity_id, network_id)</code></pre>
<p><code>spawn</code> creates a contract-declared prefab on every peer and returns the network ID. <code>transfer</code> hands authority to another player. <code>has_authority</code> is the gate every gameplay write should check. Late joiners automatically receive retained spawn state.</p>

<h2>Messages</h2>
<pre><code>local ok = NetworkSession.send("fire", { x = 1, y = 2 }, { target = "server" })
-- ok is true when the message passed contract checks and was queued</code></pre>
<p>Only contract-declared message names are accepted. The payload table must match the declared schema (finite numbers, allowed shape, size limits). The validation pipeline checks header, protocol, contract hash, epoch, sequence, size, structure, schema, sender, destination, ownership generation, and rate before delivery.</p>

<h2>Prediction and reconciliation</h2>
<p>Optional, for responsive movement on remote entities:</p>
<pre><code>NetworkSession.configure({
    input_queue_capacity = 64,
    input_future_window = 8,
    input_head_of_line_timeout = 0.5,
    input_max_per_tick = 8,
    snapshot_buffer = 32,
    interpolation_delay = 0.1,
    extrapolation_limit = 0.25,
    prediction_history_limit = 128,
    prediction_visual_decay = 0.2,
})

NetworkSession.enable_prediction({
    network_id = nid,
    input_message = "input",   -- contract message carrying inputs
    state = function()          -- return the state to replicate
        return { x = px, y = py }
    end,
    apply = function(state)     -- push an authoritative state
        Transform2D.set_position(nid, state.x, state.y)
    end,
})</code></pre>
<p>Related calls and what they return:</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.publish_snapshot()</code></td><td>Publishes the current predicted state to the host.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.predict_input(...)</code></td><td>Applies one predicted input locally.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.take_inputs()</code></td><td>Queued input array since the last call.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.prediction_state(nid)</code></td><td>Current predicted state table, or <code>nil</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.prediction_visual_offset(nid)</code></td><td>Interpolation offset to apply visually.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.remote_state(nid)</code></td><td>Last authoritative state table.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.prediction_diagnostics()</code></td><td>Counters for corrections and queue depth.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>NetworkSession.reset_prediction(nid)</code></td><td>Clears history after a teleport.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Historical 2D queries rewind the world for lag-compensated hits:</p>
<pre><code>NetworkSession.configure({
    query_history_capacity = 64,
    query_history_max_entities = 128,
    query_history_rewind_ticks = 8,
})
NetworkSession.record_query_snapshot()
local hit = NetworkSession.historical_raycast(tick, x1, y1, x2, y2)  -- hit or nil</code></pre>

<h2>Low-level transport</h2>
<pre><code>local Network = require("demi.network")

print(Network.available())          -- true when transport is compiled in
Network.host(port)                   -- ENet
Network.host_dtls(port)              -- DTLS
Network.connect(host, port)
Network.send(peer, bytes, reliable)  -- raw bytes payload
local events = Network.events()      -- connection-event array</code></pre>
<p>Use this layer for custom protocols. Most games want <code>demi.network.session</code> instead.</p>

<h2>TLS</h2>
<pre><code>local TlsServer = require("demi.network.tls.server")
local TlsClient = require("demi.network.tls.client")

TlsServer.listen(port, cert_pem, key_pem)
local ok = TlsClient.connect(host, port, { ca_certificate_pem = ca })
if not ok then print(TlsClient.error()) end

TlsClient.send(handle, payload)
local events = TlsClient.events()    -- receive queue
print(TlsClient.is_connected())      -- boolean</code></pre>
<p>TLS always verifies the certificate chain and hostname.</p>
<p><code>demi.network.crypto</code> provides <code>random_token()</code>, <code>password_hash()</code>, and <code>secure_equals(a, b)</code> for constant-time comparison.</p>

<h2>HTTP / HTTPS</h2>
<pre><code>local Http = require("demi.network.http")

local request, err = Http.post("https://api.example.com/login", {
    json = { user = "hero" },          -- JSON body + Content-Type
    headers = { ["X-Trace"] = "1" },
    timeout_ms = 10000,
    connect_timeout_ms = 2000,
    max_response_bytes = 1024 * 1024,
})
if not request then
    print("could not start request:", err)
    return
end</code></pre>
<p><code>Http.get</code>, <code>Http.post</code>, and <code>Http.request</code> (for PUT/PATCH/DELETE/HEAD) return a request handle immediately, or <code>nil, error</code> when the call could not be started. Poll the handle:</p>
<pre><code>function Game:on_update()
    if not request:done() then return end

    local response = request:response()
    if response.ok then
        -- status 200–299
        print(response.status)
        print(response.body)               -- raw string
        local data = response.json         -- parsed table, or nil + response.json_error
        if data then print(data.user) end
    else
        print(response.status, response.error, response.error_code)
    end
end</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>request:done()</code> — boolean, true when finished (success or failure).</li>
  <li><code>request:response()</code> — response table while done, <code>nil</code> while pending.</li>
  <li><code>request:cancel()</code> — abort; garbage collection also cancels.</li>
  <li>Response fields: <code>ok</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>body</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>error_code</code>, <code>json</code>, <code>json_error</code>, <code>headers</code> (lowercase names, array values).</li>
  <li>Use either <code>json</code> or <code>body</code> on the request, not both.</li>
  <li>Redirects come back as 3xx — follow them yourself if you want to.</li>
  <li>Android builds need <code>android.permission.INTERNET</code> in the project <code>build.android.permissions</code>.</li>
</ul>

